lead.memo.output:
{
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "text": "No. As of 11 July 2022, the notice showed that the Musk buyer group had exercised what it claimed was a right to terminate, not that the acquisition had ended. Musk’s counsel alleged that Twitter materially breached the agreement by failing to provide requested data on fake or spam accounts, appeared to have made misleading representations, and was likely to suffer a Company Material Adverse Effect. The notice invoked Section 8.1(d)(i).",
      "citations": [
        {
          "passage_id": "P1",
          "quote": "Twitter has failed or refused to provide this information."
        },
        {
          "passage_id": "P1",
          "quote": "appears to have made false and misleading representations upon which Mr. Musk relied when entering into the Merger Agreement, and is likely to suffer a Company Material Adverse Effect"
        },
        {
          "passage_id": "P2",
          "quote": "this letter constitutes formal notice of X Holding I, Inc.’s termination of the Merger Agreement pursuant to Section 8.1(d)(i) thereof."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Twitter called the notice invalid, denied breaching the agreement or suffering or being likely to suffer a Company Material Adverse Effect, and maintained that the agreement remained in force. The board said it intended to close at USD 54.20 per share, and Twitter reserved the right to seek specific performance to compel the buyers to fulfill their obligations. The supplied record established neither an effective termination nor a guaranteed closing.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "passage_id": "P4",
          "quote": "Mr. Musk’s and the other Musk Parties’ purported termination is invalid and wrongful"
        },
        {
          "passage_id": "P4",
          "quote": "Twitter has breached none of its obligations under the Agreement, and Twitter has not suffered and is not likely to suffer a Company Material Adverse Effect."
        },
        {
          "passage_id": "P3",
          "quote": "Twitter Board Confident in Merger Agreement and Intends to Close Transaction at $54.20 Per Share Price"
        },
        {
          "passage_id": "P4",
          "quote": "including its right to specifically enforce the Musk Parties’ obligations under the Agreement."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "filing_history": null
}

